From 1260313928a775ebcf88cb5c30f88a6104bef08f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:00:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a busy gateway-owned chat admits remote
 cards' notices to its FIFO

Remote Kanban notices reached chat 20261026_235722_bef6c6 3-63 min late on
2026-11-12 (t_01a1cff0541bf30c): only the Desktop backend's sweep delivered
them, and a chat the gateway runs turn after turn refused every pass
("deferred: a turn is running; retrying next pass", ~45 times for one card).
PR #1250 fixed the local-board leg (kanban_tui_owner); this is the remote leg.

- gateway/kanban_remote_owner.py: each notifier tick, for every live LOCAL
  chat whose ledger holds work or whose turn lease this process holds, claim
  its remote notices (kanban_remote_notices.collect) and admit them in order
  with admit_route_wake(..., "kanban-wake") as a kanban_notice card carrying
  kanban_event_keys. The claim stays in flight until a row with the key is in
  the transcript, then acked; a refused admission, or an admission dropped
  without its row, releases it (never acked). A successor after a restart
  acks by key, adopts a still-queued admission, or re-offers.
- kanban_wake_fold.card_metadata / restore / persisted user metadata carry
  kanban_event_keys onto the turn's user row; kanban_notice joins the
  producer notice kinds.
- tui_gateway/kanban_remote_fifo.py: the sweep stands aside only while a live
  gateway admission holds the notice's key.
- _RemoteWaker logs "notice row written" only when persist() wrote it,
  else "deferred".
